{# ===================================================================
   /en/claims/ — il carotaggio (10/11). Ogni claim e' una colonna che
   attraversa i cinque strati ENTIA; sotto, l'indice dei concetti. Ogni
   concetto e ogni claim hanno una pagina propria (claims-concept.njk,
   claims-claim.njk). L'elenco completo con le unita' di citazione sta in
   /en/claims/all/ (claims-all.njk). Dati: src/_data/claimPages.js.
   =================================================================== #}
{% set P = claimPages %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/carota.css">

<h1 class="cp-h1">Claims</h1>

<p class="cp-lede">A scientific claim is not a headline: it withholds itself until you have the context, and no two readers arrive with the same context. So this is not a list to scroll &mdash; it is {{ P.counts.concepts }} questions, and the claims come through them.</p>

<p class="cp-scope"><strong>These are not claims in general.</strong> Every one of them is on file because this programme stands on it, borrows a method from it, or has to answer to it. Nothing is here for completeness, and the archive is not trying to cover a field: it is showing what its own work rests on, including the parts that push back.</p>

{% if ledger %}<aside class="ld" id="ledger" aria-label="Download">
<p class="ld-k">Download · the whole set as one document</p>
<div><h2 class="ld-t">The Claims <em>Ledger</em></h2><p class="ld-d">Every claim arranged as the map, each with a permanent number, its context and its links.</p></div>
<div class="ld-l"><a href="{{ ledger.pdf }}" download>PDF</a><a href="{{ ledger.epub }}" download>ePub</a></div>
<p class="ld-m">$ edition {{ ledger.edition }} · {{ ledger.claims }} claims{% if ledger.pages %} · {{ ledger.pages }} pp.{% endif %} · rebuilt when the data change</p>
</aside>{% endif %}

<section class="cp-sec cc-wrap" id="cores" aria-labelledby="cores-h">
  <h2 id="cores-h">The claims, cored</h2>
  <p class="cp-sub">Every claim is a core drilled through the five layers of <a href="/en/entia/#claims">ENTIA</a>, from the least to the most exposed to error. Read down a column for one claim, across a band for one layer; the arcs underneath are the relations between claims.</p>
  {{ P.svg | safe }}
  <div class="cr" id="cc-read" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="cp-k">Read it</p>
    <p class="cr-hint">Point at a column, or tap it, to read one claim through its five layers. Each mark says what kind of warrant the claim lives on: <b>•</b> observed, <b>∴</b> derived, <b>∃</b> what there is, <b>!</b> what should be done. Green comes from the literature, bordeaux from the research log; a ring means the programme contests it.</p>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="cc-dati">{{ P.reader | dump | safe }}</script>

  {# sul telefono le carote si coricano: una riga per claim, sotto il Theme e il Topic che le contengono #}
  <div class="cm">
    {% for t in P.themes %}
    <h3 class="cm-th">{{ t.en }}</h3>
    {% for tp in t.topics %}
    <p class="cm-to">{{ tp.en }}</p>
    <ol>
      {% for c in tp.claims %}
      <li><a href="{{ c.url }}"><span class="n">{{ c.n }}</span><span class="c">{% for k in c.conceptsEn %}<i>{{ k.en }}</i>{% endfor %}{{ c.lead }}<small>{{ c.cite }}{% if c.names.length %} · {{ c.names | join(" · ") }}{% endif %}</small></span><span class="w" title="weight {{ c.w }}"><b style="width:{{ (c.w / 2 * 100) | round }}%"></b></span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cp-sec" id="concepts" aria-labelledby="concepts-h">
  <h2 id="concepts-h">The {{ P.counts.concepts }} concepts</h2>
  <p class="cp-sub">Layer 4 is where ideas are asserted and linked. Each concept has a page of its own: the question it answers, where it sits in the other layers, and its claims.</p>
  {% for t in P.themes %}
  <div class="ci-th">
    <h3>{{ t.en }}</h3>
    <p>{{ t.position }}</p>
    <ul class="ci">
      {% for c in t.concepts %}
      <li><a href="{{ c.url }}"><span class="nm">{{ c.en }}</span><span class="q">{{ c.question }}</span><span class="ct">{{ c.claims.length }} claim{% if c.claims.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <p class="cp-more"><a href="/en/claims/all/">All the claims, one by one &#8594;</a><a href="/en/entia/#claims">How they are classified &#8594;</a></p>
</section>

<script src="/js/carota.js" defer></script>
